#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:0
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:8
msgid "posix-mq interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"The `posix-mq` interface enables inter-process communication (IPC) messages "
"to be created, sent and received between snaps that need to use [POSIX "
"message queues](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/mq_overview.7.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:13
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:0
msgid "Permissions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:0
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:0
msgid "**no** by default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:0
msgid "**yes** with snaps from the same publisher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:0
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-super-privileged-"
"interfaces>`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:0
msgid "**no** for plugs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:0
msgid "**yes** for slots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:21
msgid ""
"The `posix-mq` plug and slot are {ref}`unsupported for parallel instances "
"<interfaces-parallel-installs-unsupported>`. Instances would perform "
"conflicting operations on the same message queues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:24
msgid "**Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:26
msgid ""
"**`posix-mq`** (slot and plug)</br> An optional identifier for a message "
"queue. Helps to identify which plugs should connect to which slots. A "
"consumer snap must use the same identifier as the provider snap in order to "
"access the message queue. It defaults to the slot or plug name respectively "
"if not specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:26
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:29
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:38
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:29
msgid ""
"**`path`** (slot)</br> Messages are shared across one or more paths, "
"depending on the requirements of the snapped applications. The path "
"attribute can either be a string, or an array of strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:32
msgid ""
"Each path must adhere to the POSIX message queue naming scheme, outlined on "
"the `mq_overview` [man page](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/"
"mq_overview.7.html):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:33
msgid ""
"Each message queue is identified by a name of the form `/somename`; that is, "
"a string of up 255 characters consisting of an initial slash, followed by "
"one or more characters, none of which are slashes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:35
msgid ""
"An array of paths should be used when the listed queues are meant to be used "
"together, as corresponding plugs will get access to all of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:38
msgid ""
"**`permissions`** (slot)</br> Defines how the messages on the queue can be "
"accessed. Can be either `read`, `write`, `create` or `delete`. Defaults to "
"`read` and `write`.  Permissions are defined on the slot side but apply to "
"the consumer plugs, while the slot side has always all the permissions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:41
msgid ""
"Any permission allows usage of the `mq_open` and `mq_getsetattr` syscalls, "
"while `read` allows `mq_timedreceive` and `mq_notify`, `write` allows "
"`mq_timedsend`, and `delete` allows `mq_unlink`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:43
msgid "Code examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:45
msgid ""
"The following definition will create a _posix-mq_ interface with read, write "
"and delete permissions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:47
msgid ""
"  test-rwd:\n"
"    interface: posix-mq\n"
"    path: /test-read-write-delete\n"
"    permissions:\n"
"      - read\n"
"      - write\n"
"      - delete\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:57
msgid ""
"The following definition will create a _posix-mq_ interface with read-only "
"permissions for multiple paths:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/posix-mq-interface.md:59
msgid ""
"  test-ro-list:\n"
"    interface: posix-mq\n"
"    path:\n"
"      - /test-ro-1\n"
"      - /test-ro-2\n"
"      - /test-ro-3\n"
"      - /test-ro-4\n"
"    permissions:\n"
"      - read\n"
msgstr ""

